    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a challenging yet fascinating subject for me. I appreciate its logical structure and problem-solving aspects, especially in algebra and calculus. While it’s not my strongest skill, I enjoy the mental exercise it provides. It’s a subject where persistence pays off, and I take pride in tackling problems step by step.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, I do experience anxiety with more complex math topics, particularly when dealing with abstract concepts or time constraints during exams. However, I’ve learned to manage it by breaking problems into smaller parts and practicing regularly. It’s a balance between frustration and satisfaction when I finally understand a concept.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I did experiment with AI tools like Khan Academy’s practice modules and online tutors for specific problems. The experience was mixed—some explanations were clear and helpful, while others felt too technical or overwhelming. I prefer a mix of human guidance and AI support for deeper understanding.",
